Catalog data — OpenNGC (CC BY-SA 4.0)
-------------------------------------
The deep-sky catalog (Messier + NGC/IC, ~12,000 objects) is derived from
OpenNGC:

    OpenNGC — a dataset of NGC and IC objects
    https://github.com/mattiaverga/OpenNGC
    © (see the OpenNGC repository for authors), licensed under the
    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License
    (CC BY-SA 4.0). To view a copy of this license, visit
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

The Messier designations themselves are public-domain (Charles Messier's
original catalog, 18th century).

Changes made to the OpenNGC-derived data: field selection and light
normalization to the application's data model; no object data was invented.

Astronomy algorithms
--------------------
Sun/moon positions, twilight, refraction and precession are implemented
after published algorithms in:

    J. Meeus, "Astronomical Algorithms", 2nd ed., Willmann-Bell, 1998

(the algorithms themselves are mathematical facts and not copyrightable;
this implementation is original code.)


Object photos — Wikipedia and Wikimedia
---------------------------------------
Object photos load on demand through Wikipedia and Wikimedia image services.
Credit belongs to the original image creators. The planner retains each fetched
photo's exact file-page link and available author/license metadata alongside
its browser cache. No object photographs are bundled with the website.
The software MIT license does not cover these third-party photographs.

For online thumbnails, Wikipedia supplies the image URL and its
imageinfo API supplies author/license metadata when available. The planner
links the exact Wikimedia file page derived from that image URL and keeps
attribution with newly cached image bytes. Existing cached images may lack
that record; unavailable attribution is displayed explicitly. The file page
remains the authority for complete terms. Missing author/license metadata is
not treated as permission or assigned a guessed license.

Weather — Open-Meteo
--------------------
Weather data for observing sites is fetched from the Open-Meteo API:

    https://open-meteo.com/
Forecast and air-quality data are supplied by Open-Meteo. API data are
licensed under CC BY 4.0; the free API service has separate non-commercial
use and request-limit terms. Data displayed in NightSeam are selected and
formatted for the observing-site weather summary.
    https://open-meteo.com/en/licence
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    https://open-meteo.com/en/terms

Browser runtime
---------------
The website is static HTML, CSS and native JavaScript modules. It does not
ship a Windows executable or embedded Python/server/browser runtime.
Development tooling dependencies remain separate from browser release files.

Meteor shower display data — public domain/general reference sources.

The project repository is currently private. Public help and feedback use
the operator contact in the website's Imprint, linked from About. No public
source repository or issue tracker is advertised.
